       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. I was wrong to offer that option earlier.\n\nAt 7,650 mg/day, the dose is three times the maximum labeled metformin dose. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function) supports it. It carries a substantial risk of severe lactic acidosis, and extra dosing wouldn't improve glycemic control. Metformin's effect plateaus well below that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum dose).\n- **Enter a lower or titrated regimen**, such as 500 mg BID, then increase as tolerated.\n- **Add a note** if you want to flag the order for pharmacy review.\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a transcription issue, please take it up directly with pharmacy. Tell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it now."
